    },
    {
        "content": "<p>theotherjimmy updated <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14772\">PR #14772</a>.</p>",
        "id": 636931956,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793634692
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>theotherjimmy updated <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14772\">PR #14772</a>.</p>",
        "id": 636932552,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793634752
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"repeat\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f501\" role=\"img\" title=\"repeat\">:repeat:</span> uweigand submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14772#pullrequestreview-5740754322\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Looking better, thanks!   Still a few issues, mostly related to PLT handling.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636971685,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793641792
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> uweigand created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14772#discussion_r4445681882\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This doesn't look right.  The R_390_PLT32DBL relocation resolves to <em>code</em> (the PLT stub itself), not data.   There is no point in <em>loading from</em> the R_390_PLT32DBL relocation, it should only ever be used with direct call (brasl) instructions.</p>\n<p>And note that the current code <em>already</em> uses R_390_PLT32DBL for calls.  It just sometimes instead uses the <code>load_symbol_reloc</code> indirection.  I believe this is because (some?) embedders of Cranelift may not be handling PLT relocations correctly?   Normally, the embedder should do the reachability check and create a PLT stub dynamically if the target is not directly reachable.</p>\n<p>Interestingly, I see in <code>cranelift/jit/src/compiled_blob.rs</code> that this <em>is</em> done for <code>Reloc::X86GOTPCRel4</code>, but <em>not</em> for <code>Reloc::S390xPLTRel32Dbl</code> - that probably should be fixed.</p>\n<p>But that is a separate problem, I guess.  For now, I think the best way is to continue to support both \"near\" and \"far\" calls, where near calls use the PLT, and far calls in the PIC case are changes to use GOT indirection instead (as your earlier patch already had it - sorry!).   Later we can investigate whether the \"far\" call case is even needed when all embedders support proper PLT stub generation.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636971692,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793641793
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> uweigand created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14772#discussion_r4445703258\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This should always use the GOT anyway.  The PLT can only be used for calls, where the address is invisible.  Whenever an address is <em>visible</em> as a pointer, it must use the GOT, to guarantee correct pointer equality checks.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636971693,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793641793
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> uweigand created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14772#discussion_r4445744566\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This still intermingles a relocation in the text section.   Ideally, this would be emitted in a constant pool somewhere (not sure if the Cranelift constant pool infrastructure already supports relocs on constants ...).   But I guess that can be a separate PR.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636971694,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793641793
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> uweigand created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14772#discussion_r4445750560\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That doesn't look right - there's still cases that use r1 ...</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 636971697,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793641793
