    {
        "content": "<p>theotherjimmy requested <a href=\"https://github.com/uweigand\">uweigand</a> for a review on <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14772\">PR #14772</a>.</p>",
        "id": 637241721,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793721154
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> uweigand submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14772#pullrequestreview-5755613293\">PR review</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The tests are now all failing, something seems to be missing.</p>\n<p>Also, minor nit inline.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 637248967,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793722368
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> uweigand created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14772#discussion_r4457316205\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>We now have explicit <code>(RelocDistance.Far)</code> above, but use a placeholder plus rule priority here.  These cases should consistently use the same method (it seems to me if we can avoid rule priorities via explicit choices, that might be preferable).</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 637248971,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793722368
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>theotherjimmy updated <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14772\">PR #14772</a>.</p>",
