    {
        "content": "<p>theotherjimmy updated <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14772\">PR #14772</a>.</p>",
        "id": 637579033,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793812769
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> theotherjimmy submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14772#pullrequestreview-5772682590\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 637579319,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793812813
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> theotherjimmy created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14772#discussion_r4470847165\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>This is to ensure that we use the PIC variant when PIC is enabled (the following line is <code>(if-let true (is-pic))</code>). I've removed the non-pic case's priority, since it's now explicit and made the PIC rules' priority 1.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 637579320,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793812813
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> uweigand submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14772#pullrequestreview-5783937023\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 637777698,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793877059
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> uweigand created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14772#discussion_r4479704665\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>What I meant is: the current code never explicitly uses matching against <code>RelocDistance.Far</code>.  Instead we always use a pair of rules, one matching against <code>RelocDistance.Near</code> and the other matching against a wildcard <code>_</code>.    There is no real difference currently, but if at any point a third member of <code>RelocDistance</code> were added, the current code would still work fine.</p>\n<p>Now, if it would make life easier, I'd be OK with changing this approach to always have some rules matching <code>RelocDistance.Far</code> and some matching <code>RelocDistance.Near</code>, but <em>no</em> wildcard in any of the rules.</p>\n<p>What this patch (still) does, however, is to add a (seemingly random?) mix of <em>sometimes</em> using <code>RelocDistance.Far</code> and sometimes using a wildcard.    Even the three -otherwise repeating- call rule blocks now use different conventions here.</p>\n<p>This is what I was asking you to fix.  Choose one strategy or the other, but then use it consistently.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 637777699,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793877060
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"memo\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4dd\" role=\"img\" title=\"memo\">:memo:</span> theotherjimmy submitted <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14772#pullrequestreview-5785574726\">PR review</a>.</p>",
        "id": 637811356,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793884890
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span aria-label=\"speech balloon\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f4ac\" role=\"img\" title=\"speech balloon\">:speech_balloon:</span> theotherjimmy created <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14772#discussion_r4480940759\">PR review comment</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Good point. I've changed all of them to implicitly match on <code>RelocDistance.Far</code> instead, since that's more general and all of them can be expressed that way.</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 637811359,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793884890
